        "content": "#include <algorithm>\n#include <cstdint>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n\n#if defined(__aarch64__)\n#include <arm_neon.h>\n#endif\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nconstexpr uint32_t MOD = 1000000007u;\n\nstatic inline void scan_unblocked_segment(uint32_t *dp, int begin, int end) {\n    int col = begin;\n    uint32_t carry = 0;\n\n#if defined(__aarch64__)\n    const uint32x4_t zero = vdupq_n_u32(0);\n    const uint32x4_t modulus = vdupq_n_u32(MOD);\n\n    for (; col + 4 <= end; col += 4) {\n        const uint32x4_t values = vld1q_u32(dp + col);\n        uint32x4_t prefix = vaddq_u32(values, vextq_u32(zero, values, 3));\n        prefix = vaddq_u32(prefix, vextq_u32(zero, prefix, 2));\n\n        // Four residues sum to less than 4*MOD, so three conditional\n        // subtractions reduce every lane without overflowing uint32_t.\n        for (int r = 0; r < 3; ++r) {\n            const uint32x4_t mask = vcgeq_u32(prefix, modulus);\n            prefix = vsubq_u32(prefix, vandq_u32(mask, modulus));\n        }\n\n        prefix = vaddq_u32(prefix, vdupq_n_u32(carry));\n        const uint32x4_t mask = vcgeq_u32(prefix, modulus);\n        prefix = vsubq_u32(prefix, vandq_u32(mask, modulus));\n        vst1q_u32(dp + col, prefix);\n        carry = vgetq_lane_u32(prefix, 3);\n    }\n#endif\n\n    for (; col < end; ++col) {\n        carry += dp[col];\n        if (carry >= MOD) carry -= MOD;\n        dp[col] = carry;\n    }\n}\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    int n, m;\n    cin >> n >> m;\n\n    vector<vector<int>> blockedCols(n);\n    for (int c = 0; c < m; ++c) {\n        int row, col;\n        cin >> row >> col;\n        blockedCols[row].push_back(col);\n    }\n\n    // In row zero, each cell is reachable only until the first blocked cell.\n    int firstBlocked = n;\n    for (int col : blockedCols[0]) {\n        firstBlocked = min(firstBlocked, col);\n    }\n    vector<uint32_t> dp(n, 0);\n    fill(dp.begin(), dp.begin() + firstBlocked, 1u);\n\n    vector<uint8_t> blockedInRow(n, 0);\n    for (int row = 1; row < n; ++row) {\n        for (int col : blockedCols[row]) blockedInRow[col] = 1;\n\n        int col = 0;\n        while (col < n) {\n            if (blockedInRow[col]) {\n                dp[col] = 0;\n                ++col;\n                continue;\n            }\n\n            const int begin = col;\n            do {\n                ++col;\n            } while (col < n && !blockedInRow[col]);\n            scan_unblocked_segment(dp.data(), begin, col);\n        }\n\n        for (int blockedCol : blockedCols[row]) blockedInRow[blockedCol] = 0;\n    }\n\n    cout << dp[n - 1] << '\\n';\n    return 0;\n}\n",
        "path": "src/solution.cpp"
      }
    ],
    "hypothesis": "A single rolling DP row removes the quadratic blocked-cell allocation and row-copy loops. Splitting each row at obstacles turns its recurrence into independent inclusive prefix scans; four-lane NEON scans can vectorize those spans while preserving the cross-block carry and obstacle reset dependencies.",
    "notes": "Uses an AArch64 NEON path with a scalar tail and scalar fallback on other architectures. The controller evaluates correctness and performance.",
